# THE POSITIVE CONTROL. Same header as the row above, but the function is
# actually CALLED -- so a DT_NEEDED on `libnolib.so` is emitted and the binary
# cannot load on any machine.
#
# This must be a COMPILE error. It used to build green and die at exec with
# `cannot open shared object file`, which the ticket calls the worst of the three
# outcomes: nothing in the build says anything is wrong.
import "nolib.h"
print(nolib_add(2, 3))
